# Default reviewers
#
# The paths below still carve out the intended working-group split (schemas,
# safety, HAL) for when the project has more than one maintainer — restore
# the `@openral/<wg>` teams once they exist. Until then every path routes to
# the sole maintainer, and `require_code_owner_review` on the branch ruleset
# (docs/contributing/development.md, "Review policy") makes this file
# load-bearing rather than decorative.
#
# GitHub does not let a PR author approve their own PR, so with a single code
# owner the sole maintainer's own PRs can never satisfy this rule through a
# normal review. That is expected, not a gap: the ruleset's
# `bypass_actors: [OrganizationAdmin]` is how the maintainer merges their own
# PRs, same as release-please's. A second code owner removes the need for it.
*                                   @AdrianLlopart

